What Happens When Two People Run terraform apply?

Terraform isn’t built for simultaneous applies. If two users run terraform apply at the same time:

What Can Go Wrong?
- State file conflicts
- Overwritten resources
- Broken infrastructure

Best Practice: Use a remote backend like S3 + DynamoDB for state locking, ensuring only one apply happens at a time.

Tip: Treat terraform apply like a production deploy—coordinate and lock!
